1
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:12,760
Who told you to run?
I'm running!

2
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,400
If you want to run, go ahead.

3
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:16,240
But remember my words well.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,680
We're done! I'm running!

5
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:23,655
I'll take care of it, sir.
You go deal with the campaign.

6
00:00:29,643 --> 00:00:31,747
So you're playing tough with me, huh?

7
00:00:41,218 --> 00:00:43,000
Hey, hey, hey!

8
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,480
Someone put a curse on me.

9
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:48,270
Go get a monk or shaman
to remove it from me!

10
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,240
Just this one job.

11
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,760
Money from this batch only.

12
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:52,280
You're set.

13
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,178
I'm not doing it.

14
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,252
I'm not here to ask you.

15
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:58,418
I'm forcing you.

16
00:01:01,587 --> 00:01:02,843
- You bastard!
- Hey, hey!

17
00:01:03,218 --> 00:01:04,880
Don't mess with my family.

18
00:01:04,966 --> 00:01:06,320
Or I'll kill you, you bastard!

19
00:01:06,424 --> 00:01:07,298
No way.

20
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,021
I know your weakness.

21
00:02:03,655 --> 00:02:04,486
Singh.

22
00:02:05,766 --> 00:02:06,553
Come here.

23
00:02:06,713 --> 00:02:07,938
Talk to me.

24
00:02:19,378 --> 00:02:20,356
Where are you going?

25
00:02:24,381 --> 00:02:25,316
Nowhere, Mom.

26
00:02:28,036 --> 00:02:30,160
Don't think I don't know your knacks.

27
00:02:30,449 --> 00:02:31,852
You're just like your father.

28
00:02:33,126 --> 00:02:35,430
People can make mistakes,
but don't make the same mistake twice.

29
00:02:35,464 --> 00:02:36,360
That's stupidity.

30
00:02:43,716 --> 00:02:44,760
If you're going to do it,

31
00:02:45,187 --> 00:02:46,707
think it through carefully.

32
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:50,640
If it's good, just do it.
So you won't regret it later.

33
00:03:00,953 --> 00:03:01,993
Yes, Mom.

34
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:07,950
Your father's.

35
00:03:08,393 --> 00:03:09,261
He hid it.

36
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,175
Keep it in case you need it.

37
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,827
I don't know how to use it.
Go figure it out yourself.

38
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,750
Today's payday.

39
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,443
I'm feeling fresh!

40
00:03:51,390 --> 00:03:52,350
Hey, Anon.

41
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:54,252
Tell them.

42
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:57,015
Right now our stuff is
the best quality on the market.

43
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,400
If they want to order more,

44
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,960
we can deliver easily.

45
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,052
But don't mention my name.

46
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,116
Yes, sir.

47
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,566
But,

48
00:04:09,796 --> 00:04:11,360
did we need this many people?

49
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:12,600
And weapons too.

50
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,110
Like we're going to war.

51
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:15,926
We're all on the same side.

52
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,012
Just in case.

53
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:20,916
Don't you know how ruthless
those Pattaya Chinese are?

54
00:04:21,452 --> 00:04:23,280
If they mess around, we'll deal with them.

55
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,587
We'll wait over there.

56
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:29,230
And you,

57
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,350
I know what you're capable of.

58
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,184
After this job,

59
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,200
it's your turn!

60
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,360
You'll learn not to mess
with someone like me.

61
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:42,430
You have the wrong idea.

62
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,840
Heavy weapons this time?

63
00:04:58,080 --> 00:04:58,793
Yeah.

64
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,184
Don't tell anyone.

65
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,406
Yeah, and your shop?

66
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:07,520
When I'm free, I'll stop by.

67
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:08,966
Yeah, see you.

68
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:26,040
(Inspector Toone)

69
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:30,984
What's up, Inspector?

70
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,803
Right now it seems Singh
and Mr. Anon are very close.

71
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,926
From their conversation,

72
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,978
they don't seem like boss and lackey.
They've worked together before.

73
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,541
But most importantly,

74
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,710
right now Mr. Anon

75
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,640
has been in contact with
the number one candidate

76
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,615
from the Meetham Party,

77
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,264
Mr. Rachin Ratchakit.

78
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:49,212
Who previously had a case
involving drug suspects

79
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,695
but the case was dismissed.

80
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,880
Keep a close watch on them.

81
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:55,033
These gangs move drugs very fast.

82
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,923
We might even be too late already.

83
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,966
Report anything immediately.

84
00:05:59,520 --> 00:05:59,800
Yes.

85
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:00,738
Lieutenant.

86
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,513
Inspector.

87
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,369
I've tracked them to the warehouse now.

88
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:07,833
Okay.

89
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:33,378
- Greetings.
- Greetings.

90
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,495
The delivery is prepared.

91
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:36,849
Check it out.

92
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,612
(Chinese)

93
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:07,320
(Chinese)

94
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,781
(Chinese)

95
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:10,849
(Chinese)

96
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:12,000
(Chinese)

97
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,040
Okay.

98
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:13,920
It's good quality.

99
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:16,135
I think it will go smoothly from here.

100
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,070
We trust you.

101
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,240
Okay.

102
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,160
So should I

103
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,812
send it all at once or...

104
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,036
split the delivery.

105
00:09:22,221 --> 00:09:25,138
(Chinese)

106
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,400
(Chinese)

107
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:29,483
(Chinese)

108
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,440
All of it.

109
00:09:30,470 --> 00:09:32,996
Mr. Liang has cleared the way
with all the authorities already.

110
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,707
Okay, good.

111
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:21,569
What does the inspector say?

112
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:22,680
They're all here.

113
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,812
Looks like a big batch delivery.

114
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,701
But Singh is gone.

115
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,600
Watch closely. Don't do anything yet.

116
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:29,852
I'm rushing over.

117
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,329
Take photos too.

118
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,609
What are you doing?

119
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,320
Inspector!

120
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:36,990
Inspector!

121
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,446
Walk out.

122
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,363
Damn it!

123
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:08,793
I knew it!

124
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:09,760
Hey, wait.

125
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,544
Let the dogs kill each other first.

126
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,458
You're clever.

127
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,400
(Chinese)

128
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,320
(Chinese)

129
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:43,720
(Chinese)

130
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:44,920
What the hell are you saying?

131
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,166
You shit face!

132
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:50,978
Gibberish yapping!

133
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:57,827
Where's Rachine?

134
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:58,707
Where is he?

135
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:04,360
They took all the drugs and
my money's there too.

136
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,018
I'm screwed!

137
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,560
These guys are fucking traitors!

138
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:08,760
He backstabbed you!

139
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,289
Liang probably

140
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:12,523
has someone else picking up
the goods from him.

141
00:12:14,141 --> 00:12:15,612
You said you dealt with him before.

142
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,206
That he could be trusted.

143
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,443
Well, this is easy for him.

144
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:19,944
He got both the drugs and the money.

145
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:24,135
Yeah, I worked with him.
But he still did this!

146
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,803
How am I supposed to explain
this to the boss?

147
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:28,166
A lifetime of work, all ruined!

148
00:12:29,544 --> 00:12:30,689
I should just run.

149
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,000
You brought all these heavy weapons.

150
00:12:33,030 --> 00:12:35,187
If you knew there'd be
a robbery, why didn't you...

151
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,658
stop them?

152
00:12:37,987 --> 00:12:40,800
The bomb, you can tell where it came from.

153
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,821
And the car, you knew they'd escape.

154
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,264
Why didn't you ambush them?

155
00:12:53,673 --> 00:12:57,667
You think I'm that stupid?
To let Anon replace me?

156
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,436
Drugs this big,

157
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,092
the cops would know.

158
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:05,089
Big agents would know there's
a big boss behind this.

159
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,855
And this time it's not me.

160
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,307
It's you.

161
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:10,953
Rachine.

162
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,926
- You're backstabbing me?
- You're backstabbing me!

163
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:17,440
- Hey!
- Either way, the target's on me.

164
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:18,840
What do you want me to do?

165
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:20,787
I need a scapegoat.

166
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:24,560
Leave behind a couple kilos of evidence.

167
00:13:24,923 --> 00:13:27,600
Some money. The cops get something,
they'll look good on the news.

168
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,821
But you're stupid.

169
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,689
And you dared to use a shaman to curse me.

170
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:35,593
Good thing I had a good doctor
help me in time.

171
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:41,458
And now you're using
an amateur kid to trick me?

172
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,676
Wait, wait, wait!

173
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:47,981
There are undercover cops everywhere!

174
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:54,750
The detectives have good eyes too.

175
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:57,440
And you'll have another case on you.

176
00:13:58,184 --> 00:13:59,532
Killing a police officer.

177
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,704
You better prepare yourself.

178
00:14:02,067 --> 00:14:03,895
Long prison sentence for sure, Anon.

179
00:14:06,461 --> 00:14:07,772
You planned all this?

180
00:14:08,043 --> 00:14:09,132
Of course.

181
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,747
Getting smarter, huh?

182
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:16,535
I'll start by shooting
this cop in the head.

183
00:14:17,710 --> 00:14:18,455
Hey!

184
00:14:59,320 --> 00:14:59,840
Toone!

185
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,120
Go!

186
00:15:46,701 --> 00:15:47,778
Hey!

187
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:49,747
Are you human or ghost?

188
00:15:49,846 --> 00:15:51,015
What do you want with me?

189
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:56,473
I hate people like you the most.

190
00:15:57,156 --> 00:15:58,172
Lying,

191
00:15:58,596 --> 00:15:59,593
deceiving,

192
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:01,113
cheating.

193
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:03,895
I've met countless people like you.

194
00:16:04,584 --> 00:16:05,920
Oh, and don't think

195
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,870
that the magic I used on you

196
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:10,923
is gone now.

197
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:37,132
Mr. Anon.

198
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:39,420
You're arrested for
distributing Class 1 narcotics.

199
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:41,446
You have the right to
remain silent or speak.

200
00:16:41,636 --> 00:16:44,898
Your statement may be used
as evidence in court.

201
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:46,738
You're an undercover cop.

202
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,393
You know I was forced.

203
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:52,012
Someone like me could never do that.
I was threatened, you saw it.

204
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,403
Actually, you're...

205
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:55,384
You can be a witness for me.

206
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:02,440
Mr. Anon.

207
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:07,341
We need to invite you to
the police station for questioning.

208
00:17:08,092 --> 00:17:08,787
Take him.

209
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:10,541
- Cuff him.
- Hey! No need!

210
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,520
- No need! I can walk!
- Cuff him!

211
00:17:12,547 --> 00:17:13,520
I said no need!

212
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,627
- Walk.
- Okay, okay!

213
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,246
I'm walking. Don't push!

214
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:17,532
Walk!

215
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:22,504
Inspector.

216
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,861
You should go to the hospital first.

217
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:26,055
This looks serious.

218
00:17:26,701 --> 00:17:27,858
I'll handle the scene.

219
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:29,372
Okay.

220
00:17:46,203 --> 00:17:46,978
Singh!

221
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:49,316
- I'm sorry.
- Yeah, we'll talk later.

222
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,609
Take care of yourself first.

223
00:17:51,138 --> 00:17:52,504
Your bleeding won't stop.

224
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:55,181
Hey!

225
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:57,723
Singh, you run first. Go, go!

226
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,049
Run first!

227
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:02,393
This case is complicated.
You'll be the only one screwed.

228
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:03,784
Run!

229
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,098
I'll get you later.

230
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,138
Go!

231
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:08,849
Go!

232
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:09,809
Go!

233
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:24,972
What a mess. Total chaos.

234
00:19:55,630 --> 00:19:57,827
I see our brothers

235
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:01,563
They are so afraid of this battle.

236
00:20:05,858 --> 00:20:07,809
Uncertain if they will survive.

237
00:20:09,476 --> 00:20:11,723
If we lose, we'll all die.

238
00:20:12,972 --> 00:20:14,849
Are you afraid of death?

239
00:20:18,436 --> 00:20:21,255
I'm more afraid of not seeing
my parents again.

240
00:20:23,864 --> 00:20:25,040
Mae Bua.

241
00:20:26,264 --> 00:20:27,563
My wife.

242
00:20:29,655 --> 00:20:33,193
Just being able to protect those I love
so they can live in peace.

243
00:20:34,166 --> 00:20:35,673
I'm willing to die.

244
00:20:37,969 --> 00:20:38,880
What about you, brother?

245
00:20:39,735 --> 00:20:40,920
Are you afraid of death?

246
00:20:42,732 --> 00:20:44,338
I died long ago.

247
00:20:46,578 --> 00:20:48,061
I died when

248
00:20:48,215 --> 00:20:51,003
the Burmese killed my wife and child.

249
00:20:53,667 --> 00:20:54,769
You know

250
00:20:56,461 --> 00:20:58,769
why they killed my wife and child?

251
00:21:01,384 --> 00:21:02,830
The villagers and I

252
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:06,990
requested troops from Ayutthaya.

253
00:21:08,947 --> 00:21:11,329
But the nobles in the capital

254
00:21:13,113 --> 00:21:16,073
never cared about the small village
where I lived.

255
00:21:17,556 --> 00:21:19,618
We were outnumbered.

256
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,563
We...

257
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:25,975
were abandoned.

258
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:28,824
To fight alone.

259
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:34,006
If the country had been united,

260
00:21:35,526 --> 00:21:38,030
my wife and child wouldn't have died.

261
00:21:48,135 --> 00:21:50,424
Do you still have faith?

262
00:21:57,513 --> 00:21:59,212
I heard that

263
00:22:00,455 --> 00:22:01,680
Bang Rachan

264
00:22:04,393 --> 00:22:06,160
didn't get the cannons

265
00:22:06,344 --> 00:22:08,363
they requested from Ayutthaya.

266
00:22:11,606 --> 00:22:13,470
This battle of ours

267
00:22:15,304 --> 00:22:17,507
will be extremely difficult.

268
00:22:22,043 --> 00:22:23,901
I have faith.

269
00:22:25,156 --> 00:22:27,643
Faith and respect in you, brother.

270
00:22:32,049 --> 00:22:34,578
That's why I came to fight with you,

271
00:22:35,292 --> 00:22:36,984
to save our nation.

272
00:22:39,187 --> 00:22:41,126
Even death won't make me regret.

273
00:22:41,649 --> 00:22:43,206
And even if I die,

274
00:22:44,978 --> 00:22:47,950
I'll become a ghost guarding
our home and country,

275
00:22:48,683 --> 00:22:52,769
hunting down the wicked
and corrupt for all eternity.

276
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:06,880
Brother, the Burmese army is coming.

277
00:24:08,250 --> 00:24:08,960
Wind.

278
00:24:09,640 --> 00:24:10,360
Water.

279
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:11,969
Fire.

280
00:24:14,516 --> 00:24:16,843
Only missing a person
of earth element.

281
00:24:53,255 --> 00:24:53,880
Stop!

282
00:24:54,080 --> 00:24:54,732
Hey!

283
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:56,129
Bring it here!

284
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:57,320
Let go!

285
00:24:57,640 --> 00:24:58,941
What are you doing?

286
00:24:59,267 --> 00:25:00,375
You tell me what you're doing!

287
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,187
Huh?

288
00:25:01,384 --> 00:25:03,538
Cutting your wrist
to kill yourself?

289
00:25:05,390 --> 00:25:08,283
No, I was just testing
if the skin is tough.

290
00:25:10,375 --> 00:25:12,701
What kind of crazy person tests
their own wrist?

291
00:25:13,544 --> 00:25:14,806
Where were you yesterday?

292
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:31,640
I don't think you've ever seen this.

293
00:25:32,683 --> 00:25:34,280
How do you know I've never seen it?

294
00:25:34,763 --> 00:25:37,249
Or never even owned it before.

295
00:25:37,378 --> 00:25:39,618
This thing is priceless.

296
00:25:39,698 --> 00:25:41,840
Hard for anyone to possess it.

297
00:25:42,012 --> 00:25:44,633
Honestly, I don't really want to
give it away.

298
00:25:45,636 --> 00:25:47,858
After owning it for so long,

299
00:25:48,406 --> 00:25:50,603
It gives me indescribable pleasure.

300
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:55,323
Hey!

301
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,033
Are you okay, Nam?

302
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:02,880
The images in my head are so clear.

303
00:26:08,920 --> 00:26:10,055
Should we see a doctor?

304
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:21,476
You're hugging too tight, I can't breathe!

305
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:22,461
Let go!

306
00:26:24,418 --> 00:26:25,550
Let go!

307
00:26:27,600 --> 00:26:28,338
You smell.

308
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:29,532
Did you shower?

309
00:26:31,212 --> 00:26:32,000
I smell.

310
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:33,200
Did I shower?

311
00:26:33,335 --> 00:26:34,812
- Yeah.
- Really?

312
00:26:35,433 --> 00:26:37,600
See, do I smell? I showered!

313
00:26:37,772 --> 00:26:39,280
- Let go!
- Shower, huh?

314
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,640
Ow! You're crazy!

315
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:41,760
Ow, ow!

316
00:26:41,784 --> 00:26:42,923
Ow, ow, ow!

317
00:26:43,009 --> 00:26:44,547
- Crazy!
- That's enough!

318
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:45,400
Enough!

319
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:46,560
They are fucking!

320
00:26:47,360 --> 00:26:48,289
Don't tease them!

321
00:26:48,590 --> 00:26:50,670
But I can't think of it any other way.

322
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:53,021
Damn, look at them in broad daylight!

323
00:26:53,390 --> 00:26:55,415
Don't they have no shame?

324
00:27:07,243 --> 00:27:09,538
Arresting people randomly,
you can get sued back.

325
00:27:10,326 --> 00:27:12,160
Think being a cop makes you above the law?

326
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:14,320
There's always someone above.

327
00:27:18,289 --> 00:27:19,956
Sorry, Mr. Anon.

328
00:27:20,480 --> 00:27:21,507
For inviting you

329
00:27:21,560 --> 00:27:22,830
to the police station for questioning.

330
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:26,615
You arrested me

331
00:27:27,427 --> 00:27:28,935
with no evidence.

332
00:27:29,384 --> 00:27:30,898
They cleared the CCTV.

333
00:27:31,950 --> 00:27:33,200
I was just tricked into being a scapegoat.

334
00:27:36,166 --> 00:27:38,166
When I'm an MP, be ready to get kicked out.

335
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:39,815
The whole station.

336
00:27:40,689 --> 00:27:41,852
So right now,

337
00:27:43,686 --> 00:27:44,836
take care of me.

338
00:27:52,627 --> 00:27:54,547
Rachine. I'm Rachine.

339
00:27:54,769 --> 00:27:57,556
People in this area know the problems well.

340
00:27:57,920 --> 00:27:59,800
Number one. Rachine, your brother.

341
00:27:59,852 --> 00:28:01,489
- Thank you.
- Brought it especially for you.

342
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:02,200
Number one.

343
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:06,756
No one knows the people
better than our own.

344
00:28:07,236 --> 00:28:10,055
Hey!

345
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:12,650
We've been in this district for long.
It's always being developed.

346
00:28:12,689 --> 00:28:15,440
For continuous progress,
don't forget to vote for the same party.

347
00:28:15,640 --> 00:28:18,080
Meetham Party, number one, Rachine.

348
00:28:18,135 --> 00:28:19,680
- Simplistic...
- and productive!

349
00:28:19,735 --> 00:28:21,320
- Simplistic...
- and productive!

350
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:23,800
- Selling well?
- All good!

351
00:28:23,852 --> 00:28:24,600
Number one.

352
00:28:24,720 --> 00:28:26,200
Number one, Mr. Rachine.

353
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:27,704
Thank you so much!

354
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:30,313
Brothers, number one!

355
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:35,347
Damn it!

356
00:28:35,396 --> 00:28:36,713
They even had undercover cops.

357
00:28:37,255 --> 00:28:38,966
You know how much I lost on this batch?

358
00:28:39,163 --> 00:28:40,523
120 million.

359
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:42,000
Totally broke, damn it!

360
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:46,073
Need to get a new batch.
Get cash to keep things moving.

361
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,504
Soon the cops will come looking for you.

362
00:28:52,750 --> 00:28:54,166
Will it lead back to us, boss?

363
00:28:55,760 --> 00:28:56,923
They'll come for sure.

364
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:59,876
Someone like Anon is a rat, damn it!

365
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:03,661
He brought in a strange motherfucker.

366
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:05,710
Bullets won't pierce it.

367
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:08,203
How far has the world gone?

368
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:09,316
Bastard!

369
00:29:09,760 --> 00:29:11,913
How do we deal with it?

370
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:15,883
Go get the hitters from Muang Phet.

371
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:17,993
Let them deal with all of them.

372
00:29:18,680 --> 00:29:20,141
Including that tattooed kid too.

373
00:29:21,692 --> 00:29:23,187
Don't let it lead back to me.

374
00:29:34,966 --> 00:29:36,018
Nam!

375
00:29:36,646 --> 00:29:37,833
Have you seen Toone?

376
00:29:38,190 --> 00:29:39,833
I called but her phone's off.

377
00:29:40,683 --> 00:29:41,563
No.

378
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:43,680
Where'd he go?

379
00:29:49,292 --> 00:29:50,596
Singh, have you seen Toone?

380
00:29:52,338 --> 00:29:53,400
Haven't seen her.

381
00:29:53,544 --> 00:29:55,704
I'll take the customers to the island.
Joe will come too.

382
00:29:55,876 --> 00:29:57,015
We'll be back this evening.

383
00:29:57,532 --> 00:29:59,212
That bastard didn't do anything.

384
00:29:59,796 --> 00:30:02,203
Then you guys put up
the high banners yourselves.

385
00:30:11,400 --> 00:30:12,000
Let's go!

386
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:21,107
Where's Singh?

387
00:30:26,929 --> 00:30:28,344
What are you guys doing here?

388
00:30:28,455 --> 00:30:29,932
Why so many?

389
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:32,960
I asked where Singh is!

390
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:49,200
So I had to hire someone
with magic to protect me.

391
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:52,695
Is that it?

392
00:30:53,052 --> 00:30:54,732
If you don't agree, then leave.

393
00:31:20,360 --> 00:31:21,261
Come here!

394
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:24,276
- Where is he?
- I don't know!

395
00:31:24,720 --> 00:31:25,889
Find him!

396
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:27,901
Looking for me?

397
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:29,636
Let go of my friend, you bastard!

398
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:31,827
Hey, Foon! Get down!

399
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:32,732
Bastard!

400
00:31:33,080 --> 00:31:34,258
Joe! Nam!

401
00:31:35,320 --> 00:31:35,880
Get in!

402
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:43,316
Did you see their guns?

403
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:45,347
Yeah.

404
00:31:45,532 --> 00:31:46,880
Damn, they wrapped them in fabric.

405
00:31:47,772 --> 00:31:48,701
I think they know.

406
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:50,627
If you get shot,
your relic can't protect you for sure.

407
00:31:52,600 --> 00:31:53,513
Bastards!

408
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:31,021
What's that sound?

409
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:31,280
Nam!

410
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:43,560
Fuck!

411
00:34:54,720 --> 00:34:56,000
Daddy! Daddy!

412
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:57,840
Daddy!

413
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:06,498
Daddy, it's me!

414
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:07,840
Damn it!

415
00:35:22,178 --> 00:35:23,126
Min!

416
00:35:23,766 --> 00:35:24,720
Min!

417
00:35:26,120 --> 00:35:26,920
I'm screwed!

418
00:35:29,193 --> 00:35:30,080
Hey!

419
00:35:39,852 --> 00:35:41,452
I told you you had the wrong idea.

420
00:35:43,027 --> 00:35:45,058
Just do what I tell you.

421
00:35:45,981 --> 00:35:47,840
Aren't you scared at all, huh?

422
00:35:48,200 --> 00:35:49,156
You people.

423
00:35:50,840 --> 00:35:52,276
Above the law.

424
00:35:53,640 --> 00:35:54,855
What do you want?

425
00:35:55,040 --> 00:35:55,661
Huh?

426
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:56,449
Money?

427
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:57,089
Power?

428
00:35:57,175 --> 00:35:58,996
Women? Drugs? Tell me!

429
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:02,935
Why do you keep messing with me?
What do you want? Tell me!

430
00:36:06,240 --> 00:36:06,947
One,

431
00:36:08,301 --> 00:36:09,741
you didn't obey me.

432
00:36:10,344 --> 00:36:11,415
Two,

433
00:36:11,796 --> 00:36:14,264
you challenged my authority.

434
00:36:14,886 --> 00:36:16,061
Three,

435
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,821
I just don't like your face.

436
00:36:18,520 --> 00:36:19,440
Damn it!

437
00:36:19,870 --> 00:36:21,630
You don't like my face?

438
00:37:21,316 --> 00:37:23,483
I was at the shop with Joe.

439
00:37:24,178 --> 00:37:25,901
Suddenly customers came in.

440
00:37:26,227 --> 00:37:27,956
I told them the shop wasn't open yet.

441
00:37:29,446 --> 00:37:32,356
Have you seen these customers before?

442
00:37:33,710 --> 00:37:34,732
Never seen them.

443
00:37:34,843 --> 00:37:36,061
I don't know them.

444
00:37:37,033 --> 00:37:39,120
When they arrived,
they fought among themselves.

445
00:37:39,649 --> 00:37:41,138
Shot each other up.

446
00:37:42,338 --> 00:37:44,203
Good thing I survived.

447
00:37:45,606 --> 00:37:47,895
My friend Joe had nothing to do with it.

448
00:37:48,012 --> 00:37:49,243
Let him go.

449
00:37:51,040 --> 00:37:51,852
Foon!

450
00:37:52,055 --> 00:37:53,304
- Auntie!
- How are you?

451
00:37:54,412 --> 00:37:55,741
What about Joe?

452
00:37:57,796 --> 00:37:58,713
He's in...

453
00:37:58,843 --> 00:38:00,024
the holding cell.

454
00:38:01,895 --> 00:38:02,886
Mom!

455
00:38:03,329 --> 00:38:04,640
Can you hear me, Mom?

456
00:38:04,843 --> 00:38:06,098
Get me out, Mom!

457
00:38:06,203 --> 00:38:07,563
I don't want to be in here!

458
00:38:07,655 --> 00:38:11,027
A well-bred person like me
shouldn't be in here, Mom!

459
00:38:11,483 --> 00:38:14,769
Mom, get me out!
On Mother's Day I'll ordain for you!

460
00:38:15,120 --> 00:38:15,840
Officer,

461
00:38:15,993 --> 00:38:17,556
I'm here to bail him out.

462
00:38:18,160 --> 00:38:18,769
Okay.

463
00:38:18,892 --> 00:38:21,581
- Just a moment.
- Get me out! I don't want to be here, Mom!

464
00:38:22,720 --> 00:38:25,495
I don't want them to get up
and bite my neck, Mom!

465
00:38:43,409 --> 00:38:45,107
So you remember now, Nam?

466
00:38:47,390 --> 00:38:48,504
I remember.

467
00:38:49,889 --> 00:38:51,021
My name is Min.

468
00:38:51,520 --> 00:38:53,255
I was Mr. Narong's bodyguard.

469
00:38:54,356 --> 00:38:56,566
Trained to do all the shady work.

470
00:38:58,960 --> 00:39:00,886
Actually, I remembered a while ago.

471
00:39:02,024 --> 00:39:03,624
Just wasn't sure

472
00:39:03,753 --> 00:39:05,267
if it was a dream

473
00:39:05,723 --> 00:39:07,132
or reality.

474
00:39:09,150 --> 00:39:11,076
But you just killed several people.

475
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:16,086
I've killed more than that.

476
00:39:18,763 --> 00:39:20,104
So what now?

477
00:39:22,547 --> 00:39:24,221
I need that book.

478
00:39:27,720 --> 00:39:29,175
Why do you need the book?

479
00:39:30,172 --> 00:39:32,227
Shouldn't we find a place to hide now?

480
00:39:35,089 --> 00:39:36,584
I don't think we should run.

481
00:39:36,996 --> 00:39:37,975
Because even if we run,

482
00:39:38,049 --> 00:39:39,489
they'll find us.

483
00:39:50,978 --> 00:39:53,298
Those whose magics never lose power

484
00:39:53,421 --> 00:39:57,415
are those who have all four elements:
earth, water, wind, fire

485
00:39:57,495 --> 00:39:59,760
combined in one person.

486
00:40:00,332 --> 00:40:02,953
That person will be eternally strong,

487
00:40:03,187 --> 00:40:05,938
impossible to defeat.

488
00:40:09,883 --> 00:40:11,400
The Satra Sutra book,

489
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:12,849
whoever possesses it

490
00:40:12,984 --> 00:40:14,240
will be superhuman,

491
00:40:14,535 --> 00:40:16,440
immortal in spirit.

492
00:40:16,676 --> 00:40:18,160
But to open it,

493
00:40:18,280 --> 00:40:21,421
you need the blood of someone
born on the 9th day of the 9th month.

494
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:22,560
Elements:

495
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:23,569
Earth,

496
00:40:23,640 --> 00:40:24,120
Water,

497
00:40:24,840 --> 00:40:25,320
Wind,

498
00:40:26,080 --> 00:40:26,843
Fire.

499
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:51,636
And finally, they found it.

500
00:40:53,960 --> 00:40:55,704
Don't let them get all

501
00:40:55,889 --> 00:40:58,073
earth, water, wind, and fire.

502
00:40:58,781 --> 00:41:00,520
People can be deluded
and intoxicated

503
00:41:00,615 --> 00:41:02,006
by evil,

504
00:41:02,135 --> 00:41:03,400
seeing wrong as right.

505
00:41:03,581 --> 00:41:05,840
People will bow to them.

506
00:41:06,363 --> 00:41:09,507
Evil will reclaim faith

507
00:41:09,753 --> 00:41:11,747
in their wickedness.

508
00:41:13,692 --> 00:41:15,156
And goodness,

509
00:41:15,483 --> 00:41:17,360
doesn't it have anything
for people to have faith in?

510
00:41:18,449 --> 00:41:20,578
Goodness is hard to do.

511
00:41:21,243 --> 00:41:23,538
But if you do good,

512
00:41:23,753 --> 00:41:26,633
goodness will bear fruit in itself

513
00:41:26,781 --> 00:41:28,200
and will create faith

514
00:41:28,258 --> 00:41:29,932
in goodness.

515
00:42:13,520 --> 00:42:15,000
Carried by the wind,

516
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:17,778
from the Khmer with the wind.

517
00:42:18,080 --> 00:42:19,735
Singh, your son,

518
00:42:19,800 --> 00:42:21,895
was born on the 9th of the 9th month.

519
00:42:23,840 --> 00:42:27,747
His father intended to pass down
this dark magic

520
00:42:27,840 --> 00:42:29,163
through bloodline.

521
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:32,867
But dark elements outnumber light elements.

522
00:42:33,335 --> 00:42:36,221
Your husband fell into the dark magic arts

523
00:42:36,680 --> 00:42:38,375
and couldn't pull himself out.

524
00:43:05,400 --> 00:43:07,772
- Hey!
- Mom! It's Singh!

525
00:43:14,120 --> 00:43:15,360
What are you doing, Mom?

526
00:43:16,400 --> 00:43:18,301
Who knew you'd come?

527
00:43:25,101 --> 00:43:26,664
If you know you did wrong,

528
00:43:26,818 --> 00:43:28,381
go turn yourself in.

529
00:43:29,298 --> 00:43:31,581
Running now means
running for the rest of your life.

530
00:43:33,747 --> 00:43:35,046
Think carefully.

531
00:43:35,618 --> 00:43:37,513
You're grown up now. Decide for yourself.

532
00:43:40,412 --> 00:43:43,089
As for Foon and Joe, they were bailed out.

533
00:43:45,200 --> 00:43:47,169
Where are you two going to hide?

534
00:43:49,778 --> 00:43:51,390
I'm thinking of discussing
with the monk teacher.

535
00:43:51,507 --> 00:43:53,021
staying at the temple for a night.

536
00:43:53,600 --> 00:43:55,883
Can Nam stay at a temple?

537
00:43:57,064 --> 00:43:58,030
Yes.

538
00:43:59,944 --> 00:44:01,249
We'll see first, Mom.

539
00:44:01,735 --> 00:44:02,812
If we can't stay,

540
00:44:03,636 --> 00:44:05,156
we might go to another province.

541
00:44:07,907 --> 00:44:09,895
Should you go stay at Uncle Pong's
in Lamphun?

542
00:44:13,003 --> 00:44:14,375
Probably not, Mom.

543
00:44:14,609 --> 00:44:16,098
Don't want to bother Uncle Pong
for no reason.

544
00:44:20,135 --> 00:44:22,529
Nam seems off. She looks strange.

545
00:44:23,027 --> 00:44:24,430
Not talkative like before.

546
00:44:27,649 --> 00:44:29,480
Well, let's eat first.

547
00:44:29,686 --> 00:44:31,187
I'm about to make kaprao.

548
00:44:31,920 --> 00:44:32,683
Let's eat, Mom.

549
00:44:32,880 --> 00:44:33,661
I'm hungry.

550
00:44:46,480 --> 00:44:47,446
Who are you?

551
00:44:47,800 --> 00:44:48,683
Who are you looking for?

552
00:44:53,513 --> 00:44:54,941
Looking for your son.

553
00:45:01,507 --> 00:45:02,320
How did you get in?

554
00:45:02,440 --> 00:45:03,870
I didn't let you in.

555
00:45:04,160 --> 00:45:05,440
I'm calling the police.

556
00:45:06,067 --> 00:45:06,950
Go ahead.

557
00:45:08,280 --> 00:45:09,809
All the police in this province can come.

558
00:45:39,009 --> 00:45:40,080
What are you doing?

559
00:45:40,184 --> 00:45:41,070
Hmm?

560
00:45:46,280 --> 00:45:47,378
Come sit and talk.

561
00:45:47,883 --> 00:45:48,615
Come.

562
00:46:01,113 --> 00:46:03,421
Do you know what your son has done?

563
00:46:05,003 --> 00:46:06,320
He's caused a lot of trouble.

564
00:46:06,440 --> 00:46:07,335
Your son.

565
00:46:14,375 --> 00:46:15,310
Where is he?

566
00:46:15,360 --> 00:46:16,800
Your son, huh?

567
00:46:20,560 --> 00:46:21,378
He's not here.

568
00:46:23,230 --> 00:46:24,898
There are three glasses.

569
00:46:25,809 --> 00:46:26,516
One,

570
00:46:26,960 --> 00:46:27,560
two,

571
00:46:27,880 --> 00:46:28,443
and

572
00:46:29,040 --> 00:46:29,720
three.

573
00:46:37,673 --> 00:46:38,873
He went out.

574
00:46:50,104 --> 00:46:51,760
I'm looking for someone.

575
00:46:53,224 --> 00:46:55,716
The first one with the water element,
I found.

576
00:46:57,446 --> 00:46:59,390
The second one,

577
00:47:02,295 --> 00:47:06,190
with the wind element,
I think I'll find soon.

578
00:47:10,227 --> 00:47:12,307
The third one,

579
00:47:12,941 --> 00:47:14,369
earth element.

580
00:47:19,950 --> 00:47:21,409
Is the one

581
00:47:21,766 --> 00:47:25,335
with the most powerful magic.

582
00:47:27,587 --> 00:47:32,350
The one known as the legendary,
demon slaying necromancer.

583
00:47:42,523 --> 00:47:44,640
The third one is interesting.

584
00:47:50,375 --> 00:47:51,889
I'm still finding him.

585
00:47:57,704 --> 00:48:00,110
But today I didn't come to ask for help.

586
00:48:22,510 --> 00:48:23,458
Where is he?

587
00:48:33,920 --> 00:48:34,520
I don't know.

588
00:48:34,600 --> 00:48:35,790
Hm, say that again.

589
00:48:47,640 --> 00:48:48,769
I don't know.

590
00:48:51,267 --> 00:48:52,338
Even if I knew,

591
00:48:54,123 --> 00:48:55,735
I wouldn't tell you.
